            ]
          },
          "worked": "For the left branch, $x\\le1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-(x-1)-2\\\\y&=-x-1\\end{align*}$$\nFor the right branch, $x\\ge1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x-1)-2\\\\y&=x-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe branches have gradients $-1$ and $1$ and meet at $(1,-2)$. Draw the upward V through the intercepts $(-1,0)$, $(3,0)$ and $(0,-1)$, and label both branch equations.",
